## Why This Is Asked
Tests a novel fixed-gap non-crossing pairing constraint, a natural extension of classic non-crossing matching problems, while probing DP state design and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- DP over prefixes with fixed pair distance
- Non-crossing/disjoint constraint handling
- Backpointers for reconstruction
- Space/time optimization trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxFixedGapPairs(A, d, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-Infinity));
  const take = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(false));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
      dp[i][t] = dp[i - 1][t];
      if (t > 0 && i - d - 1 >= 0) {
        const cand = dp[i - d - 1][t - 1] + A[i - 1] * A[i - d - 1];
        if (cand > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = cand;
          take[i][t] = true;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  const pairs = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0 && i > 0) {
    if (take[i][t]) {
      pairs.push([i - d, i]); // 1-based indices of the pair
      i = i - d - 1;
      t--;
    } else {
      i--;
    }
  }
  pairs.reverse();
  return { value: dp[n][k], pairs };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests a practical DP over partitions with a non-trivial subproblem (distinct counts) and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- DP over contiguous partitions
- Precomputation of distinct counts for all subarrays
- Backpointers for block reconstruction

## Code Example
```javascript
// Distinct counts precomputation
for (let l = 0; l < n; l++) {
  const freq = new Map();
  let dist = 0;
  for (let r = l; r < n; r++) {
    const x = logs[r];
    if ((freq.get(x) || 0) === 0) dist++;
    freq.set(x, (freq.get(x) || 0) + 1);
    distinctCount[l][r] = dist;
  }
}

// DP
for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) dp[i][1] = distinctCount[0][i-1];
for (let t = 2; t <= k; t++) {
  for (let i = t; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let j = t-1; j < i; j++) {
      const val = dp[j][t-1] + distinctCount[j][i-1];
      if (val > dp[i][t]) { dp[i][t] = val; par[i][t] = j; }
    }
  }
}
```

